      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Normal color vision is made possible by specialized cells in the retina
    called cone cells.\nThere are three types of cones:\n\nL-cones \u2013 sensitive
    to red light\n\nM-cones \u2013 sensitive to green light\n\nS-cones \u2013 sensitive
    to blue light\n\nThe brain compares the signals from these three cones to create
    millions of different colors.\nWhen all three cone types function properly, color
    perception is accurate and detailed."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: d1728ba5990034831bbe01f3a2578b70, type: 2}
